## Native variadic functions (ImplementationPlan.md 5.15.2 'Link time
## (msil-ld)' rules 2-6, 5.14.8, 5.10.7, 5.10.11; M26.d; recon p3 variadics
## 2.4, 4 and 8.2). The backend expands every call of an undefined variadic
## function over a native-layout va_list (ExpandVariadics): the reference
## carries VARARG with FixedParams, and its IL signature is the fixed
## parameters followed by one native int. msil-ld binds such a reference
## natively to the function's va_list variant, found in the native index
## only:
## - the P/Invoke keeps the C name and gets the variant as its entry, with the
##   expanded signature: 'pinvokeimpl("libc.so.6" as "vprintf" nomangle
##   cdecl) int32 'printf'(native int, native int)' in linked text, entry
##   'vprintf' in the image, through a CIL object, an LTO image and
##   --lto-emit-asm text alike; --print-imports shows
##   'printf -> libc.so.6!vprintf [function, <version>]' (rule 6);
## - the C runtime of the link (rule 5): linux-gnu Glibc (printf -> vprintf),
##   windows-gnu Msvcrt (printf -> vprintf in msvcrt.dll), windows-msvc UCRT,
##   which has no variants, and windows-gnu whose C runtime identity (the
##   first -l named ucrt, ...) is ucrt: UCRT too;
## - a natively bound VARARG reference without a variant in the table is
##     native function '<f>' (<module>) is variadic and has neither a va_list
##     variant nor an entry in the fixed-arity list
##   (a library's own variadic function, clone, printf on UCRT); one whose
##   variant no native library defines is
##     native function '<f>' (<module>) is variadic, and its va_list variant
##     '<vf>' is not defined by the native libraries
##   also when the program defines a function of the variant's name itself:
##   a program's own MSIL vsprintf never captures sprintf, and a program's own
##   vprintf leaves printf bound to the native vprintf (rule 2). msil-ld never
##   falls back to a fixed-arity P/Invoke for an expanded call;
## - a function on the triple's fixed-arity list (open on glibc, scanf in
##   msvcrt.dll) is called with fixed arity per call site (FIXED_ARITY,
##   5.14.8): one P/Invoke per IL signature, entry the C name, no variant
##   (rule 3);
## - a variadic declaration with an explicit import module is fixed-arity too
##   (5.10.7 and M26.c's 'Explicit imports'): one stub per call-site
##   signature, bound unchecked although no native library defines it;
## - the address of a natively bound variadic function is, until M28,
##     the address of native variadic function '<f>' (<module>) is not
##     supported for MSIL yet
##   (rule 4).
## Every error is the only one of its link, has no phase number and leaves no
## output; the retired Phase 2 texts (VARARG in Signatures, native variadic
## calls) never appear.

